message.content:
This is a Halloween decoration, which falls under festive articles in heading 9505. Subheading 9505.10 covers Christmas articles, and 9505.90 covers other festive, carnival or other entertainment articles. Halloween items go under 9505.90. The statistical suffix for "other" is 9505.90.6000 (other festive articles, other than Christmas).

Electrical, animated Halloween decorations have been classified in 9505.90.6000 in CBP rulings. 9505.90.40 covers "Articles for Halloween" in older versions, but I don't think that is current. The current 9505.90 has 9505.90.20 (confetti, etc.), 9505.90.40 (Halloween masks?), and 9505.90.60 (other). I believe 9505.90.6000 is the right choice.

{"hts_code": "9505.90.6000", "reason": "A plug-in, animated, sound-and-light Halloween mummy figure sold solely as a Halloween decoration is a festive article of heading 9505, classified in the residual subheading for other festive articles (9505.90.6000)."}
